{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":1,"result":{"protocolVersion":"2025-11-25","capabilities":{"tools":{}},"serverInfo":{"name":"medaka","version":"0.1.0-preview"}}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":2,"result":{"tools":[{"name":"medaka_check","description":"FIRST CHOICE over shelling out to `medaka check` for any type-check/diagnostic query: returns the same structured JSON `medaka check --json` emits (stable `code`, `range`, `severity`, `help`, and a machine-applicable `fix` where available) — act on it directly instead of parsing CLI text. Provide exactly one of `file` or `source`.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","description":"Path to a .mdk file to check."},"source":{"type":"string","description":"Inline Medaka source to check (no file on disk)."}}}},{"name":"medaka_type_at","description":"FIRST CHOICE for \"what type is this\" instead of re-deriving it by hand — infer the type/scheme at a position (stateless hover). Give `file` plus 0-based `line`/`col` (LSP-style); returns `<name> : <type>`. Off any identifier returns a clean \"no symbol\" note, not an error.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the .mdk file to query."},"line":{"type":"integer","description":"0-based line of the position (LSP-style, first line is 0)."},"col":{"type":"integer","description":"0-based column of the position (LSP-style, first column is 0)."}},"required":["file","line","col"]}},{"name":"medaka_symbols","description":"FIRST CHOICE for a file's outline instead of grepping for `data`/`impl`/`fn` headers — lists top-level declarations with source ranges. Give `file`; parse-only, so it works even on a file with type errors. One entry per multi-clause function, not one-per-clause. A parse failure returns a distinct `{\"parseError\":true,\"line\",\"col\",\"message\"}` isError, never a silently-empty list.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the .mdk file to list symbols for."}},"required":["file"]}},{"name":"medaka_definition","description":"FIRST CHOICE for \"where is X defined\" WITHIN THIS FILE instead of grepping — go-to-definition. Give `file` plus 0-based `line`/`col`. INTRA-FILE ONLY: a name defined elsewhere returns empty — reach for `medaka_references` on a cross-file lookup instead.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the .mdk file to query."},"line":{"type":"integer","description":"0-based line of the position (LSP-style, first line is 0)."},"col":{"type":"integer","description":"0-based column of the position (LSP-style, first column is 0)."}},"required":["file","line","col"]}},{"name":"medaka_references","description":"FIRST CHOICE for \"find every use of X\" instead of grep — resolves by BINDER IDENTITY, not spelling, so it is correct under shadowing, import aliasing, and same-name-in-different-modules, where grep is not. Give `file` plus 0-based `line`/`col`; optional `includeDeclaration` (default true). Project-wide, read-only; never descends into stdlib bodies.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the .mdk file to query."},"line":{"type":"integer","description":"0-based line of the position (LSP-style, first line is 0)."},"col":{"type":"integer","description":"0-based column of the position (LSP-style, first column is 0)."},"includeDeclaration":{"type":"boolean","description":"Include the symbol's own declaration site in the result. Default true."}},"required":["file","line","col"]}},{"name":"medaka_fmt","description":"FIRST CHOICE for formatting Medaka source instead of shelling out to `medaka fmt`. Provide exactly one of `file` or `source`. NEVER writes to disk — apply the returned text yourself. Pass `check: true` for a clean/dirty verdict only (no full text).","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","description":"Path to a .mdk file to format. READ ONLY — the file is never written; the formatted text is returned for the caller to apply."},"source":{"type":"string","description":"Inline Medaka source to format (no file on disk)."},"check":{"type":"boolean","description":"If true, report clean/dirty instead of returning the formatted text (default false)."}}}},{"name":"medaka_lint","description":"FIRST CHOICE for style-linting Medaka source instead of shelling out to `medaka lint`. Give `paths` (array of file paths); narrow with comma-separated `deny`/`only`/`disable`. Report-only (no autofix) — same diagnostic schema as `medaka_check`.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"paths":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Paths to .mdk files to lint."},"deny":{"type":"string","description":"Comma-separated rule names to promote to error severity (mirrors --deny)."},"only":{"type":"string","description":"Comma-separated rule names to keep, dropping findings from every other rule (mirrors --only)."},"disable":{"type":"string","description":"Comma-separated rule names to suppress (mirrors --disable)."}},"required":["paths"]}},{"name":"medaka_test","description":"FIRST CHOICE for running a file's doctests/property tests instead of `medaka test` via Bash. Give `file`. ⚠️ RESULTS ARE UNDER THE INTERPRETER (eval), NOT the native backend — report as \"passes under eval\", never unqualified (#81). Bare `test \"…\"` decls are NOT run here.","inputSchema":{"type":"object","properties":{"file":{"type":"string","description":"Path to the .mdk file whose doctests (and property tests, if any) to run."}},"required":["file"]}}]}}
{"jsonrpc":"2.0","id":3,"error":{"code":-32601,"message":"Unknown tool: bogus_tool"}}
